assert.equal(mod.matchRoute('/users/:id', '/Users/42'), null);
assert.equal(mod.matchRoute('/users/:id/orders', '/users//orders'), null);

drills.explanation:
Normalise the path (drop the query, drop one trailing slash), compare segment counts, then walk both lists:

```js
if (w.startsWith(':')) {
  if (h === '') return null;
  try { params[w.slice(1)] = decodeURIComponent(h); } catch { return null; }
} else if (w !== h) {
  return null;
}
```

Decoding per segment AFTER splitting matters: decoding the whole URL first would turn an encoded `%2F` inside an id into a real `/` and change the segment count.
